    "event": "Severe Thunderstorm Warning",
    "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
    "senderName": "NWS State College PA",
    "headline": "Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued September 3 at 12:52AM EDT until September 3 at 1:30AM EDT by NWS State College PA",
    "description": "At 1252 AM EDT, severe thunderstorms were located along a line from\nover Ralston to over Snow Shoe, or along a line from 20 miles north\nof Montoursville to 11 miles northwest of Bellefonte, moving\nsoutheast at 45 mph.\n\nHAZARD...60 mph wind gusts and small hail.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Expect damage to roofs, siding, and trees.\n\nLocations impacted include...\nWilliamsport, Lock Haven, J",
    "instruction": "Seek shelter inside a well-built structure and stay away from\nwindows. These storms are capable of producing damaging winds.\n\nTornadoes can develop quickly from severe thunderstorms. Seek shelter\nimmediately in an interior room on the lowest floor of a well-built\nstructure.\n\nTorrential rainfall is also occurring with these storms and may lead\nto flash flooding. Do not drive your vehicle through flooded\nroadways.",
    "response": "Shelter",
    "note": null,
